    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d267-a2">

                <pb facs="0613" n="607" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg607"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in inclosure 1 in No.
                    15.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Stevens to Mr. Dole.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-01-17"><hi rendition="#italic">January 17,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Think Capt. Wiltse will endeavor to maintain order and protect life and property,
                    but do not think he would take command of the men of the Provisional
                    Government.</p>
                <p>Will have him come to the legation soon as possible and take his opinion and
                    inform you as soon as possible.</p>
                <p>Yours, truly,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John L. Stevens.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
